==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|in|lang=la}} {{term|versō|lang=la}} {{term|foliō||on the turned leaf, on the turned page|lang=la}}, the [[ablative]] of the Latin {{term|versus||turned, changed|lang=la}} from the perfect passive participle of {{term|vertō||turn|lang=la}}. Compare {{term|rēctus||right|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɜː(ɹ)səʊ|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The back side of a flat object which is to be examined visually, as for reading, such as a sheet or a leaf or a [[coin]] or a [[medal]].
# {{context|printing|lang=en}} The [[left-hand]] [[page]] of a [[book]] of a script which reads from left to right, usually having an even page number.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|back side of a flat object}} [[back#Noun|back]], [[flipside]]

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|back side of a flat object}} [[recto]], [[obverse]]

